<title>UK: Royal Sun cut lowered at SBC Warburg.</title>
<headline>Royal Sun cut lowered at SBC Warburg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Royal &amp; Sun Alliance Plc dropped on Thursday in a rising UK insurance sector as SBC Warburg cut the stock to &quot;add&quot; from &quot;buy,&quot; dealers said.</p>
<p>The stock was down 6p at 482-1/2 by 1305 GMT in trade of 3.3 million shares, even as other leading general insurers were squeezed higher.</p>
<p>Analysts at SBC Warburg were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
